NEARS-1754 QA — terms-link tap does not navigate on a real device (widget test is a false positive)

Screen: UserApp Sign Up (mobile branch), sign_up_widget.dart -> ConditionCheckBoxWidget(forDeliveryMan: true)
Device: emulator-5554, density 480 (3.0x), English/LTR

Repro (reproduced 3x with fresh uiautomator dumps each time):
1. uiautomator dump reports "Terms & Conditions" link node:
   content-desc="Terms & Conditions" checkable="false" clickable="true"
   bounds="[156,1866][955,1932]"  (center = 555,1899; 266x22dp @3x density)
2. adb shell input tap 555 1899   (exact center of the link's own reported bounds)
3. Result: checkbox toggles ("I Agree..." node checked flips true<->false),
   NO navigation occurs (screen content unchanged, no RouteHelper.termsAndCondition push).
4. Repeated at left edge of the text (200,1899) and at (500,1945, still inside the
   44dp checkbox row but below the link's 22dp-tall bounds) — same result every time:
   checkbox toggles, never navigates.

Expected (per ticket AC + code comment in condition_check_box_widget.dart claiming
"GestureDetector WidgetSpan ... correctly wins the tap"):
   tapping the terms link text navigates to Terms & Conditions WITHOUT toggling the checkbox.

Contrast: the widget test
  UserApp/test/features/auth/condition_check_box_widget_a11y_test.dart
  "tapping the terms link navigates WITHOUT toggling the checkbox"
PASSES using tester.tap(find.text('terms_conditions')) — this does not reproduce the
real-device gesture-arena outcome. The live device shows the opposite of what the
pinned test asserts, for the identical logical control.

Secondary, related finding: the link's own effective tap target is only ~22dp tall
(266x22dp @3x density) vs AC3's required >=44dp floor — but since it never navigates
at all right now, the sizing gap is secondary to the total loss of function.
